`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Substring: 14% of bytes, not documents"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Net: about 75% of documents removed"}),`
`]})]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Deduplication counts documents until a stage removes bytes",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The first two stages remove whole documents, so document counts describe what enters and leaves them. Each percentage is of that stage's own input. MinHash removes 23% of the 12.8B documents that exact deduplication left. The net removal compares the 9.8B survivors with the 38.7B documents that entered. The third stage changes the unit. Fuzzy suffix-array substring removal deletes repeated spans inside documents, so bytes are its natural unit. It also deletes short spans that sit between two repeated ones. After it, the report gives 9.7B documents and 36.5T bytes ",e.jsx(s,{id:"ettinger2025olmo3",children:"Ettinger et al., 2025"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["One pair of figures does not line up. The report gives 38.8B documents after the heuristic filters and 38.7B entering exact deduplication, in the same section. It does not explain the 0.1B difference ",e.jsx(s,{id:"ettinger2025olmo3",children:"Ettinger et al., 2025"}),". The funnel starts the deduplication stage at the 38.7B."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The funnel draws each stage in its own unit. Its document segment runs from the heuristic filters to the 9.8B documents left after MinHash, and the substring stage follows as a separate, derived segment in bytes. A unit change breaks the geometry: widths in documents and in bytes cannot share one axis, so a single funnel through all four stages would look precise and be wrong."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Mixing needs the same care. A mixture decides how often each document is sampled, which is exposure, so it needs a separate ledger from the survival counts of this funnel."})]})]})]}),`
`,e.jsx(l,{tab:"Beyond Web: Code",children:e.jsxs(a,{reading:!0,title:"Code needs a front end of its own",accent:4,number:"18",items:"4",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
