`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["Compare data choices at a fixed budget. DCLM fixes the model architecture, the training recipe, the token budget and the evaluation and varies only the dataset, which shows that data alone moves benchmarks ",e.jsx(s,{id:"li2024dclm",children:"Li et al., 2024"}),". Report the exposure accounting with every comparison, so that a gain from repetition is not credited to filtering. Recipes from different labs change many things at once, so they show which decisions exist without isolating the effect of any one of them."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Keep pool, release and mix apart. Pool, release and mix are three different numbers, and documents, bytes, tokens and sampled exposure are four different units. Code needs its own front end: license detection, programming-language identification and repository grouping have no web counterpart, and secret redaction parallels web PII filtering."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"A learned filter rewards resemblance to chosen positives. The classifier's positive class defines what its score measures, so choosing the positives decides what counts as quality. The scored tiers can survive into mixing."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"LSH proposes, exact Jaccard decides. MinHash with LSH bands proposes candidate pairs. Exact Jaccard similarity, the clusters of verified pairs and the keep-one rule decide which documents stay."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["A claim about synthetic data holds for one recipe and one stage. Nemotron-CC adds rewritten text to pretraining ",e.jsx(s,{id:"su2024nemotroncc",children:"Su et al., 2025"}),", and so does FinePhrase ",e.jsx(s,{id:"niklaus2026finephrase",children:"Niklaus et al., 2026"}),". OLMo 3 excludes synthetic rephrasing from its main pretraining mix ",e.jsx(s,{id:"ettinger2025olmo3",children:"Ettinger et al., 2025"}),", and so does MAI ",e.jsx(s,{id:"microsoftai2026maithinking1",children:"Microsoft AI Team, 2026"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["Mixing is an optimization. The objective is the average bits per byte over a task suite, and a surrogate fitted from a proxy swarm stands in for it. The repetition budget is the constraint, and the solution is pulled back toward the natural mix ",e.jsx(s,{id:"chen2026olmix",children:"Chen et al., 2026"}),"."]}),`
`]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The exercise repeats that design: it builds the filtering and deduplication path, chooses a domain mix and compares the result against the provided unfiltered baseline at the same budget. This week's Anki cards feed Quiz 5."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Week 10 turns from training a model to serving it. It schedules many requests at once and counts the memory that each request's KV cache takes."})]})]}),e.jsx(a,{title:"To-dos until next week",accent:7,number:"47",children:e.jsxs("div",{className:"flex flex-col gap-10",children:[e.jsx("div",{className:"flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-24 gap-y-6",children:e.jsxs("figure",{className:"text-center",children:[e.jsx("a",{href:"https://tally.so/r/7XKjZ9",children:e.jsx("img",{src:"images/qr-week-09-muddiest-point.svg",alt:"QR code for the muddiest-point survey, tally.so/r/7XKjZ9",className:"w-56 h-56"})}),e.jsxs("figcaption",{children:[e.jsx("strong",{children:"Muddiest point"}),e.jsx("br",{}),"Do it right now! (2 min)"]})]})}),e.jsxs("div",{className:"grid gap-x-12 gap-y-6 md:grid-cols-3",children:[e.jsxs("div",{children:[e.jsx("div",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Before the tutorial"}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
